course: dictionary
lesson: 12281
title: Bruise or contusion?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A contusion is the doctor's word for a bruise. You get one when you knock or bump your body hard enough that the skin is not cut, but tiny blood vessels under it leak blood and make a dark mark.
explain: «Sam bumped his knee on the table, and by the next morning it had turned purple.» The skin did not split, so Sam has a contusion. The clues are bumped, which means knocked, and purple, a colour bruises often turn.
explain: Doctors and nurses use contusion in hospital reports and first-aid books. «The nurse checked the contusion on his arm.» In everyday talk we say bruise, and the two words mean the same thing. Use whichever fits your writing.
fact: Contusion is a noun, and its plural is contusions.
fact: «Contusion» means a bruise: the skin is not broken, but blood leaks under it and makes a dark mark.
fact: A bruise often changes colour as it heals, from dark purple to green, then yellow.
fact: Phrases you may read include «a bone contusion», «cuts and contusions» and «minor contusions».
fact: A cut breaks the skin, but a contusion does not.
exercise: «The footballer got a nasty contusion on his shin.» What is a contusion? | A cut that bleeds | A broken bone | *A bruise | A sore throat
exercise: The doctor said the mark on Ella's arm was a contusion. Which word means the same? | *Bruise | Scab | Blister | Graze
exercise: Ava says, «The contusion on my leg has gone yellow.» What does that tell you? | It is brand new and needs stitches | It has nothing to do with the skin | It is broken and bleeding badly | *It is healing
test: Tom fell off his bike. His skin was not cut, but a dark mark came up on his leg. What injury did Tom get? | Burn | *Contusion | Sprain | Cut
test: Which of these is a contusion? | A cut where the skin has split open | *A dark mark where the skin is not broken, after a knock | A sneeze that sounds like a cough | A splinter in your finger
exam: The report says «minor contusions» on the arm. What does minor mean here? | *Small | Bloody | Broken | Serious
